---
import Signature from './Signature.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<section id="about" class="section section--alt">
  <div class="wrap about">
    <div class="about__portrait">
      {/* A studio shot of her actually working would outperform this eventually —
          buyers connect with the maker mid-process. Good enough to launch on. */}
      <img
        src="/images/jenifer-mazer-headshot.jpg"
        alt="Jenifer Mazer, artist and party designer, smiling outdoors on a sunny day"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        width="768"
        height="1024"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="about__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h2>Meet Jen</h2>

      {/*
        DRAFT BIO — written from her work, not from knowing her.

        Everything below is grounded in things visible in her photographs: what
        she paints, what she bakes, how she works. I have deliberately not
        invented biography — no hometown, no training, no "since 2015", no
        family details. Those would read as facts and be wrong.

        It should still be replaced with her own words. The About section is the
        second-most-read part of a site like this after the gallery, and hers
        will convert better than mine.
      */}
      <p>
        Jen designs parties the way she paints — one piece at a time, by hand,
        until the whole thing holds together. A baby shower banner lettered in
        pink and blue with clouds painted around the edges. Unicorn cookies
        iced one at a time, each mane a slightly different colour. A dessert
        table where the cookies, the cupcakes and the sign all came out of the
        same sketch.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's the part most people notice afterwards: it matched. Most parties
        get assembled from four different shops and it shows. Hers don't,
        because one person made all of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The painting came first and still runs underneath everything else —
        citrus against deep navy, koi turning through blue water, a pumpkin
        ringed in sunflowers. Same hand, different subject. It's why her parties
        look drawn rather than ordered.
      </p>
      <p>
        She works out of {site.location.city} and across Palm Beach County,
        and she takes the small ones. There's no minimum to hit before she'll
        pick up the phone.
      </p>

      <Signature height="3.25rem" color="var(--navy)" class="about__sig" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .about__portrait {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    background: var(--cream-deep);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  }

  .about__portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .about__sig {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .about__sig { color: var(--lemon) !important; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .about__portrait { max-width: 420px; }
  }
</style>
